Mathematical Architecture: Pivot-Independent Orbital Alignment Model (PIOAM)

Your revised framework establishes three interacting systems:

* Parallelism: Two or more orbital processes operate simultaneously.

* Periodicity: Those processes repeat within defined temporal and rotational intervals.

* Convergence: Independent orbital processes reach a mathematically verifiable synchronization condition.

The central distinction is that two orbital objects do not need to occupy identical positions to establish synchronization. They need a measurable relationship between their position, direction, phase, accumulated weight, and temporal progression.

This makes the model suitable for the HI–ME–LO architecture and the Sol Chrono Recognition system.

